<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Hlubi Chiefdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1873 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A northern Nguni chiefdom scattered in the wars of the early 19th century, remembered for Langalibalele's 1873 confrontation with colonial Natal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Hlubi were an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> chiefdom settled near the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buffalo-river-kwazulu-natal">Mzinyathi</a> (Buffalo) river in what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>. By the late 18th century, under Bhungane, they were among the larger chiefdoms of the region.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hlubi chiefs ruled over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-herding homesteads, and their royal house was famed for rainmaking. Around 1818 the Hlubi were attacked by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom">Ngwane</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a>; one section under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpangazitha">Mpangazitha</a> fled onto the highveld and fought in the wars of the 1820s. Others later settled in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natal-colony">Natal</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/langalibalele">Langalibalele</a>, a renowned rainmaker.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1873 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/langalibalele">Langalibalele</a> refused to register guns his men had earned at the diamond fields; the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/natal-colony">Natal</a> government declared him in rebellion, broke up the Hlubi location and sent him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robben-island">Robben Island</a>. The Hlubi chieftaincy was later restored.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1700 CE – 1873 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:3.44%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1873 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bhungane, Mpangazitha, Langalibalele</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Nguni religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>isiZulu (Hlubi)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hlubi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1786&amp;focus=hlubi-chiefdom" aria-label="Hlubi Chiefdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5302 3270 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hlubi Chiefdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5791 3515h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5622 3526h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5622 3526h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day South Africa. <a href="/atlas?year=1786&amp;focus=hlubi-chiefdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

